Found porting idol's fixes (2026-10-24). Under mawk, the default awk on Debian and Ubuntu, the gsub that writes \(em in `pidly man` (bin/pidly ~4418) produces \\(em, so the man page differs from docs/pidly.1 and `pidly check` always reports it out of date there. Use a replacement mawk and gawk agree on (for example build the string outside gsub, or use & escaping that both read the same).


Also BSD awk (macOS, 20200816): `pidly check` there reports docs/pidly.1 out of date for the same \\(em doubling (seen 2026-10-24).
